# Services and API Layer

- Keep HTTP/client logic in services; avoid direct network calls in screens/components.
- Use typed request and response contracts for service methods.
- Normalize API errors into predictable, UI-safe objects/messages.
- Keep URL and header construction centralized; avoid repeating endpoint fragments.

## Reliability

- Handle timeout/network failures explicitly.
- Keep retry logic deliberate and bounded; avoid infinite retries.
- Do not swallow errors silently; propagate meaningful context to state layer.
